ev_volatility":0.20861607752056605,"_gp_rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":54.7,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":-0.13972661011843057,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":4,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":44.4,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":-0.06525100333324207,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":13.9,"_gate_rev_durability":0.11708716728311108,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":83.5,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.019518006816159988,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":32.8,"_gate_share_shrink":0.049037039891638434,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.011969632979326116,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":80.1,"_gate_insider_own":0.05348,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":35.7,"_gate_insider_buying":0.75,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":75.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"ConnectOne Bancorp, Inc. operates as the bank holding company for ConnectOne Bank that provides commercial banking products and services for small and mid-sized businesses, local professionals, and individuals in the United States. The company offers personal and business checking, money market, and time and savings accounts; credit cards, wire transfers, safe deposit boxes, automated teller services and telephone, and internet and mobile banking. It also provides retirement accounts, consumer and cash management services for business clients, including treasury direct, automated clearing house origination, remote deposit capture, and digital invoicing. In addition, the company offers consumer and commercial business loans, including lines of credit, commercial and residential mortgages, home equity and bridge loans, and other personal loans; commercial loans secured by collateral, such as business assets including accounts receivable, inventory and equipment, and mortgages filed on commercial and residential real estate, as well as cash balances and marketable securities. Further, the company provides real estate loans, which includes loans secured by first liens on completed commercial properties, including multifamily properties, to purchase or refinance properties; residential mortgages, such as loans secured by first liens on 1-4 family and condominiums; and cooperative residential real estate loans. The company was formerly known as Center Bancorp, Inc. and changed its name to ConnectOne Bancorp, Inc. in July 2014. ConnectOne Bancorp, Inc. was incorporated in 1982 and is headquartered in Englewood Cliffs, New Jersey.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Frank S. Sorrentino III | Chairman & CEO | Age 63 | Compensation: $2.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 750 people. Revenue per employee of $518K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 16%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $135K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $6K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10). Recent headlines include layoff or workforce-reduction announcements.","financial_summary":["ConnectOne Bancorp, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $1.6B market cap on $388M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +7% over the past three years and +12% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 9% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The business throws off $101M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 26 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.32\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 0.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 2.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 5.3% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins softening -1.2pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.043266301035953345},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Recent layoff news \u2014 often the market\u2019s first signal that growth is under pressure or costs are being rebased","sev":"amber","cat":"news"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["31 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Avoiding Lag: Real-Time Signals in (CNOB) Movement","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/43/Avoiding_Lag:_Real-Time_Signals_in_CNOB_Movement_111026125002_1794333002.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794333002.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.823,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"ConnectOne Bancorp (CNOB) Stock Looks Cheap On Its 106% Run","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nasdaq-cnob/connectone-bancorp/news/connectone-bancorp-cnob-stock-looks-cheap-on-its-106-run","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794302385.603,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.888,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"What Is Drawing Attention To ConnectOne Bancorp (CNOB) Today?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nasdaq-cnob/connectone-bancorp/news/what-is-drawing-attention-to-connectone-bancorp-cnob-today","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793763918.037,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.542,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Earnings Update Might Change The Case For Investing In ConnectOne Bancorp Stock (CNOB)","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nasdaq-cnob/connectone-bancorp/news/earnings-update-might-change-the-case-for-investing-in-conne","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793666275.025,"origin":"tiing